   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "אָמְרוּ לוֹ לְרַבִּי עֲקִיבָא: הֵיכָן מָצִינוּ כּוּ׳. וְלָא?! וַהֲרֵי נְמָלָה! בְּרִיָּה שָׁאנֵי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: The Rabbis «said to Rabbi Akiva: Where do we find» that one who eats any amount is liable, leading you to say that this person is liable? The Gemara asks: «And» do we «not? But isn’t» one who eats «an ant» liable, despite the fact that it is smaller than an olive-bulk? The Gemara answers: A whole «entity is different,» since it has significance."
  }
